 for colour by kind, type, spacing and grid, shape radii and strokes, connector styles and arrowheads, zones, key, title block and source line, plus the first-glance accent), how compose_board.py, the composer and the claude.ai Project mirror would read it, how safe defaults hold when a user edits it badly (validation, contrast floors, fallbacks), and how the quality rubric and the board scorecard would check a board against it. Name what the current boards already do well so nothing good is removed. Every iteration either covers a new part of the design surface, a new diagram type or a new outside source, or deepens an earlier finding and names the iteration it builds on. Cite every claim as [SOURCE: path:line], and name the screenshot file for a visual finding. The synthesis ranks at least 10 design changes, at least 3 of them on consistency across diagram types, each naming the file it changes and its evidence, and ends with a concrete recommendation for the design spec file. Never open AI Systems/Product Context, any Barter board, board URL or Figma file key, and never quote Barter product flows.
